epartment of Oncology, The First Affiliated Hospital, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Zhang Y", "lastName": "Zhang", "firstName": "Yujie", "initials": "Y", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "School of Basic Medical Sciences, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}, {"affiliation": "Key Laboratory of Environment and Genes Related to Diseases, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Ministry of Education, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Liu C", "lastName": "Liu", "firstName": "Chengcheng", "initials": "C", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "School of Basic Medical Sciences, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Zhang M", "lastName": "Zhang", "firstName": "Mingzhen", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4686-6526"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "School of Basic Medical Sciences, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}, {"affiliation": "Key Laboratory of Environment and Genes Related to Diseases, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Ministry of Education, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Han S", "lastName": "Han", "firstName": "Suxia", "initials": "S", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0842-3908"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Oncology, The First Affiliated Hospital, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4686-6526"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6795-8235"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0842-3908"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "16", "journalIssueId": 3092260, "dateOfPublication": "2021 ", "monthOfPublication": 0, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Int J Nanomedicine", "title": "International journal of nanomedicine", "essn": "1178-2013", "issn": "1176-9114", "isoabbreviation": "Int J Nanomedicine", "nlmid": "101263847"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "1083-1102", "abstractText": "Radiotherapy (RT) is a cancer treatment that uses high doses of radiation to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors. Although great success has been achieved on radiotherapy, there is still an intractable challenge to enhance radiation damage to tumor tissue and reduce side effects to healthy tissue. Radiosensitizers are chemicals or pharmaceutical agents that can enhance the killing effect on tumor cells by accelerating DNA damage and producing free radicals indirectly. In most cases, radiosensitizers have less effect on normal tissues. In recent years, several strategies have been exploited to develop radiosensitizers that are highly effective and have low toxicity. In this review, we first summarized the applications of radiosensitizers including small molecules, macromolecules, and nanomaterials, especially those that have been used in clinical trials. Second, the development states of radiosensitizers and the possible mechanisms to improve radiosensitizers sensibility are reviewed. Third, the challenges and prospects for clinical translation of radiosensitizers in oncotherapy are presented.", "affiliation": "Department of Oncology, The First Affiliated Hospital, Xi'an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, Shaanxi, 710061, People's Republic of China.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic-eCollection", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "des